fn declassify(
        &mut self,
    )

description:
Implement a method that declassifies a value by downgrading the security labels of four designated components.

The method takes a mutable reference to the current value state. It may only be called when the existing value state is well-formed.

After the method completes:

- the labels at positions 1, 2, 3, and 4 must each be changed to `Symbol`;
- the overall value must become constant;
- the underlying value structure must be preserved except for the permitted changes to labels and value sets, i.e. the resulting state must be equal to the old state with its value sets and labels updated to the current ones;
- the resulting state must still be well-formed.

In other words, this operation performs a controlled declassification of the four labeled components while preserving the rest of the value’s specification and invariants.

